38c93b61 (59 1793053577711 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing guard") (src . "test: the change-stream guard masks the store identity in check's answer\n\ncheck now answers an instance clause with the store's device and inode,\nand those differ between any two store directories by construction: the\nguard's base and tree run on two copies, so GUARD-2 read every check\nanswer as an unlisted difference once the expect file was emptied, red\nagainst master itself.\n\nThe guard masks the two numbers in that clause and nothing else. It\nworks on data, not text: the answer is read as one datum and its stdout\nas exactly one check datum; each two-element (device <exact integer>)\nand (inode <exact integer>) field directly under the instance clause\nbecomes the integer 0, so a change of type still shows; strings are never\nlooked into; the answer is rewritten only when its text is exactly what\nwriting its datum gives, with its ending kept, and is otherwise left byte\nfor byte, so spacing, quoting, newlines and extra datums still compare.\nTwo rows pin the mask and its limits: the clause masked while other\nnumbers stay; a nonce or a machine string holding such text, a sibling\nfield, another verb's clause, a payload, a non-integer value, a device\nthat became a string, a lost inode and a doubled space all still differ.\n\n- test/change-stream-guard.sc: store-identity, GUARD-0 and GUARD-0b.\n- test/rows-baseline.txt: change-stream-guard 6 rows, 13 lines.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 485))))
